---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { OutcomeBalance } from "../components/AnalysisCharts.tsx";
import stats from "../data/dataset-stats.json";
---

<Layout title="Story — Diabetes Capstone">
  <div class="px-8 py-8 space-y-8 max-w-3xl">
    <header>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-blue-600 uppercase">
        Unit 8 · Data Storytelling — data + visuals + narrative
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-1">The Quiet Drift</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-100">
      <h2 class="font-semibold mb-2">Setting the scene</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
        {stats.rows} health records. {stats.healthy} people without diabetes,{" "}
        {stats.diabetic} with it. Same clinics, same tests — two different
        futures hiding in eight numbers.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <OutcomeBalance
          healthy={stats.healthy}
          diabetic={stats.diabetic}
          client:load
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-100">
      <h2 class="font-semibold mb-2">Rising action — the numbers whisper first</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
        Nobody wakes up diabetic. Glucose creeps from a healthy median of{" "}
        {stats.features.Glucose.healthy.median} toward the diabetic median of{" "}
        {stats.features.Glucose.diabetic.median}. BMI edges from{" "}
        {stats.features.BMI.healthy.median} to{" "}
        {stats.features.BMI.diabetic.median}. Each step feels normal — until
        enough of them point the same way.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-red-200">
      <h2 class="font-semibold mb-2">Climax — the bad zone</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
        We drew a line around where confirmed diabetics live: every metric at
        or above the diabetic median. Cross into that zone on several metrics
        at once, and our model — trained on these very records — starts
        flashing 60% and above. That is the moment to act, months or years
        before a diagnosis would.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-100">
      <h2 class="font-semibold mb-2">Resolution — watch the drift, not the day</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
        One reading is noise; a trajectory is a story. The{" "}
        <a href="/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">My Tracking</a> tab
        plots your own line against the bad zone and warns while the drift is
        still reversible — with a coach that suggests the next three small
        steps. Data explained what happened. Narrative decides what happens
        next.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
